@.str.s10192 = private unnamed_addr constant [1245 x i8] c"\0A    Compiler-development commands:\0A      prismio runtime-hash\0A      prismio dump-ast <source.psm>\0A      prismio aif <source.psm> [--manifest] [--summary] [--layout] [--copyable-collections]\0A                               [--theta-fields] [--budget=N] [--target <triple>]\0A      prismio aif <source.psm> --why=<ID|symbol>   explain one allocation decision\0A      prismio build|aif <source.psm> --force-layout=<Type>:<hot>   emit a named layout candidate\0A      prismio build <source.psm> --verify | --debug\0A\0A          --debug is the zero-analysis level and says nothing about debug info;\0A          --verify builds with the allocation ledger.\0A\0A          check --overlay reads <file.psm>, wherever the program reaches it, from\0A          the file <text> instead -- an editor's unsaved buffer; repeat it for each\0A          unsaved file. --partial type checks what parsed, holding back errors that\0A          only the unparsed text caused. Check a module\0A          through its program's entry, since a module uses names its program\0A          shares: `prismio check src/main.psm --overlay src/parse/stmt.psm buf`.\0A          --module names a module checked on its own, as its importers name it:\0A          `prismio check std/map.psm --module std.map`.\0A    \00"
